WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:03.990
- I think the two biggest
influences on Midnight Mass,

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:04.823
that I can think of,

00:00:04.823 --> 00:00:06.920
are both out of Stephen King's universe.

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:09.080
- I'm Trevor Macy and
this is Mike Flanagan.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:11.780
Our Midnight Mass is currently
streaming on Netflix,

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:14.113
and this is going to
be laden with spoilers.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:19.943
(spooky suspenseful music)

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:25.930
- Salem's Lot is a story
about a small New England town

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:27.960
that is infiltrated by a vampire,

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.100
and it was King's riff on Dracula.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:33.430
And the entire ensemble is kind
of systematically converted

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:36.740
until the town has been
turned against itself,

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:38.850
and you're watching the
destruction of a community.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.220
Storm of the Century is
also worth mentioning

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:44.860
because it features an
isolated island community,

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:46.620
and this tiny community braces

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:48.810
for this once-in-a-century storm.

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:51.140
And with the storm comes a stranger,

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:53.750
who immediately starts
to disrupt everything.

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:57.090
At the center of that is
the sheriff of the island,

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:00.110
who is not only the moral
center of that community,

00:01:00.110 --> 00:01:03.590
but is also tasked with having
to deal with this newcomer.

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:05.420
And now that I'm saying it out loud, boy,

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:07.265
there's some Needful Things in here too.

00:01:07.265 --> 00:01:08.170
(Trevor laughs)

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:11.273
So yeah, it's all Stephen
King, all the time.

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:15.690
Bev Keane is the monster of Midnight Mass.

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:17.260
For all the other monsters at play,

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:18.960
she's the one I think is the scariest.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:20.340
In a lot of ways,

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:25.340
she's a very similar character
to Mrs. Carmody in The Mist,

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:28.523
who I think is a
phenomenal King antagonist.

00:01:28.523 --> 00:01:31.670
- We are being punished for what?

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:34.750
For going against the will of God.

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:35.970
- The thing about Bev Keane though,

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:40.310
is she's also drawn a lot
out of real life right now.

00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:41.595
Bev Keane is Karen.

00:01:41.595 --> 00:01:42.860
(dog barks)

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:45.570
- Snapped at me! Snapped right at me!

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:48.380
- But I think even before that,
everybody knew a Bev Keane.

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:49.213
- Yeah.

00:01:49.213 --> 00:01:52.340
The sad part is that Samantha
Sloyan, who plays Bev Keane,

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:54.210
is, like, the nicest person in the world.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:57.550
And forever, I feel like she's
gonna walk down the street

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:58.961
and people are going to be like ugh.

00:01:58.961 --> 00:02:03.700
- Or Beverly fucking Keane's
queen evil bitchin', poor him.

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:05.980
- I think we'll have to just
issue a continual apology

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:08.070
to her for getting pushed off the sidewalk

00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:08.960
for the rest of her life.

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:13.960
- Do not cherry pick the glories of God!

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.190
- I was raised Catholic.

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:19.764
So the Catholic iconography
is very much kind of woven

00:02:19.764 --> 00:02:21.100
into my DNA.

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:24.170
And how I first saw the horror genre

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:26.470
because the scariest examples of horror

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:29.180
that I can recall
experiencing first in my life,

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:30.230
I found in the Bible,

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:32.710
where you have rivers of blood,

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:36.190
and angels coming to the
door to slaughter children,

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:39.260
and pillars of fire,
and all sorts of horrors

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:43.510
that are just baked into the Bible itself.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:44.680
As a young Catholic,

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.930
that was incredibly impactful on me.

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:50.550
I think Midnight Mass
is not a vampire story

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:54.070
in the traditional sense
because the vampire in our story

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:58.311
is really representing
fanaticism and fundamentalism.

00:02:58.311 --> 00:03:00.410
We didn't use the word "vampire"

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:02.930
because the minute you do,
the minute you say that,

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:05.900
it changes the story into a vampire story.

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:07.090
The word "vampire" carries

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:11.060
with it hundreds of
years of horror fiction

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:13.350
and tropes and expectations.

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:16.310
- Not everybody has the same
idea of what that means,

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:19.060
but what no one has in their heads,

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:21.120
if you just use that word,

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:23.260
is the totality of how that mythology

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:25.160
is used in Midnight Mass.

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:27.410
- And I think we were way more interested

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:29.470
in a modern parable about faith

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:31.900
and about the corruption
that fundamentalism

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:34.550
and fanaticism can have
on any belief system,

00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:36.220
outside of religion.

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:38.370
Horror deals with monsters,

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:40.750
and the monsters that
are the most entertaining

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:44.700
are the vampires and the
werewolves and the zombies.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:48.007
There are these other entities
that infiltrate our world

00:03:48.007 --> 00:03:52.809
and how we brave humans fight
them is one of the staples

00:03:52.809 --> 00:03:53.910
of the genre.

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:57.030
The zealotry on display in Midnight Mass

00:03:57.030 --> 00:03:59.090
is particularly interesting to me

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:01.695
because while we have a vampire

00:04:01.695 --> 00:04:04.525
who infiltrates this community,

00:04:04.525 --> 00:04:09.525
the vampire isn't the thing
that tears this community apart.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:12.460
The community is... It's the people

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:15.940
who suddenly find their
belief systems validated.

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:19.975
That kind of fanaticism and
fundamentalism represents,

00:04:19.975 --> 00:04:23.970
I think, the potential for
how monstrous we can be

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:24.910
to each other.

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:27.050
The only thing that stops us

00:04:27.050 --> 00:04:28.840
from treating each other that way

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:31.090
and inflicting these horrors
on each other is an ability

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:31.940
to empathize.

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:33.720
Once that's taken away,

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:35.760
that's what frees human beings

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:38.660
to commit unspeakable
acts against each other.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:41.290
And that, I think, is the scariest horror

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:42.240
that I can imagine.

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:48.090
Midnight Mass has been
the most personal story

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:49.340
that I've ever gotten to tell.

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:53.090
And it's been that way for me
for many years at this point.

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:57.270
The story that has given me
a chance to explore issues

00:04:57.270 --> 00:05:02.270
with my existence, my sobriety, my faith.

00:05:02.281 --> 00:05:07.281
The fact that it resonated
with my other collaborators,

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:11.190
that it resonated with Trevor
on just as personal level,

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:13.600
with our other writers, with our cast.

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:17.010
There's something about
wondering what it means

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:20.990
to be alive on this world
and what happens after we die

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:23.330
that is universal.

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:26.090
These questions unite people.

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:28.820
- The body stops a cell at a time,

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:32.090
but the brain keeps firing those neurons.

00:05:32.090 --> 00:05:35.850
- Even though the answers to
these questions divide people.

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:37.700
- I strongly suspect that the audience

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:40.720
will make it theirs in
the same way that I did

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:42.660
and our cast did and
our other writers did.

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:45.930
You know, even though it is
Mike's most personal work.

00:05:45.930 --> 00:05:47.320
- Thanks for watching Netflix Geeked.

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:49.420
Midnight Mass is now streaming on Netflix.

